--- !u!114 &1602589099
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1602589097}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color>  <b>Runtime API:</b> InventoryComponent.AddItemById
    / DropSelected / Save, ExplosiveForce.Explode(), Spawner.StartSpawn / StopSpawn,
    Selector.Next / Previous, InteractiveObject events.\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color> 
    <b>Scene workflow:</b> First Person Controller (1) = PlayerController3DPhysics
    + InventoryComponent, InventoryHand, InventoryDropper, Selector; Physics = zones
    and interactables; NPC = AiNavigation / NpcNavigation prefabs on a NavMeshSurface.\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color> 
    <b>Verification:</b> WASD + mouse to walk, E interacts, walk into the spheres
    to pick them up, 1 / 2 switch the hand slot, G drops the held item. Esc frees
    the cursor (to collapse this card).\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color>  Physics/Cube:
    PhysicsEvents3D onTriggerEnter / Exit -> SpawnerCars.StartSpawn / StopSpawn +
    particles on / off\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color>  Magnetic = MagneticField (attract
    / repel cycle), Impulse Zone = ImpulseZone (pushes bodies away from its center)\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color> 
    Explosive Interactive Sphere (2): InteractiveObject (E) -> ExplosiveForce.Explode()\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color> 
    Interactive Sphere (1): E -> VisualToggle.Toggle -> Terrain renderer on / off\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color> 
    Keys: MultiKeyEventTrigger 1 / 2 -> Selector.Previous / Next = the InventoryHand
    slot\n<color=#40C9F0>\xBB</color>  Pickups: PickableItem + InventoryPickupBridge
    fill the inventory, Inventory (InventoryView) lists it; saved under NeoDemo.Adventure.Inventory"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
  m_fontMaterials: []
